abstract: "Computer-assisted proof candidates for Open Questions 6.2 and 6.4 of C. Gaiser, Restricted generalized Schur numbers (arXiv:2608.08789): S_3(k;2) = k^3+3k^2+2k-2 for every k >= 3; the exact thresholds K(3),...,K(10) = 3,4,6,7,8,9,10,11; S_2(12;11) = 915; the two-colour weak Schur numbers WS_8(2)=365, WS_9(2)=505, WS_10(2)=676; and K(l) >= l+2 for l >= 24. Not peer reviewed."
